# This repository checks its own integrity by sha256 (tools/skill-hashes.txt), so the working tree
# has to agree byte for byte on every machine. Git's line-ending normalisation would rewrite every
# LF on a Windows checkout, change the bytes, and make check_links.py report that the read-only
# skills had been edited — on a clone where nobody touched them.
#
# So: LF in the working tree everywhere, and no conversion at all for the files whose bytes are the
# guarantee.

* text=auto eol=lf

# The skill instruction files are copied byte-identical and verified by hash. Never normalise,
# never diff. This is deliberately narrow: it matches SKILL.md and any sibling .md directly beside
# it, and nothing deeper. Since the 2026-08-22 layout change everything a skill owns lives under
# .claude/skills/ too — methods, examples, profiles, shared tools — and that is ordinary source
# which has to stay readable in a diff.
.claude/skills/*/*.md -text -diff

# _shared/ holds no SKILL.md, so it is not a skill and its documents are not hash-verified.
.claude/skills/_shared/*.md text diff

# Binary assets: the voice prompt WAVs are immutable conditioning identities.
*.wav binary
*.png binary
*.mp4 binary

# The Claude Design bundles are stored byte-exact, not as text. Normalisation would rewrite every
# LF in a 26 MB generated file and change its hash — and the two copies of the explainer bundle
# differ by exactly one byte (`captions:true` -> `false`), which is the claim that would be lost.
# The films' picture cannot be re-rendered without these files.
*.html -text -diff
